{#
  Generic reusable "edit this rich text field" icon button — the trigger
  half of the pair described in partials/rich_text_field.html.twig's doc
  comment. save_url is normally the generic core endpoint
  (Core\Http\Controller\EditableContentController::updateField(), POST
  /api/rich-text-content, role_min admin) — no per-module save endpoint
  needed for the text itself.

  That role_min is deliberately less strict than the Configuration menu:
  this endpoint is never authorized by being in that menu, it is
  authorized by the host page embedding this button — and every such page
  is a role_min: admin page of the Espace chefs d'U menu. At superadmin it
  refused the chief d'unité those pages are for, on save only, after the
  text had been typed.

  The calling PAGE (not this partial, to avoid duplicate DOM ids) must
  once, anywhere on the page:
  - {% include 'partials/rich_text_editor.html.twig' %}
  - <script src="{{ asset('/assets/js/rich-text-field.js') }}" defer></script>

  Usage:
  {% include 'partials/rich_text_edit_button.html.twig' with {
      content_key: 'banner_content_' ~ item.id,
      save_url: '/api/rich-text-content'
  } %}
#}
<button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary rich-text-field-edit-btn"
        data-key="{{ content_key }}" data-save-url="{{ save_url }}" title="Modifier" aria-label="Modifier">
    <i class="bi bi-pencil" aria-hidden="true"></i>
</button>
